{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Will YHWH be pleased</b> — If I can offer Him many cattle, for He desires thousands of rams and ten thousand rivers of oil, or if I would give Him firstborn, <b>for my transgressions</b>, that He forgive me. And the meaning of <b>I will offer Him</b> is that I have nothing with which to appease Him except animals or children." "<b>The fruit of my body</b> — The phrase is duplicated, and the bet in <b>for ten thousand</b> serves two words after it. And likewise: <b>I would give the firstborn of my body for my transgressions, for</b> the sin of my soul — like <i>ויעבד ישראל באשה</i> (Genesis 29:18, \"Israel served for a woman\")."], :book :micah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {1 "Ibn Ezra's text reads 'Israel' instead of 'Jacob' in the Genesis citation; translated as found."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Micah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=20&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:14:08.103892901Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}